Quick FAQs
Q.1: What is the main function of a welding manipulator?
Ans: It automates torch movement - vertical, horizontal, and rotational - to produce consistent welds on large or cylindrical workpieces, reducing manual error and welder fatigue.
Q.2: What's the difference between a welding manipulator and a positioner?
Ans: A manipulator moves the welding head; a positioner rotates or tilts the workpiece itself. Most SAW setups use both together. For larger applications, a Headstock and Tailstock Positioner can provide controlled support and rotation of the workpiece during welding.
